    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFixes #62134 by adding early configuration validation for `ngram_gpu` speculative decoding when compilation is explicitly disabled.\n\n## Claims\n\n*   **Bug Fix:** Prevents a fatal engine initialization crash when `speculative_config.method=\"ngram_gpu\"` is paired with `compilation_config.mode=\"NONE\"`.\n*   **UX Improvement:** Intercepts the invalid configuration early in `create_engine_config()` and provides an actionable `ValueError` directing the user to either enable compilation or use the CPU `ngram` proposer.\n\n## Validation\n\n*   Verified against the reproduction script provided in #62134.\n*   Initializing an `LLM` with the conflicting configs now cleanly raises the target `ValueError` during configuration setup, rather than crashing with an obscure `ValueError: No compilation mode is set` deeply inside `GPUModelRunnerV1.__init__`.\n\n## Details\n\n**Root Cause:** The `ngram_gpu` kernel unconditionally wraps itself in `TorchCompileWithNoGuardsWrapper`, which requires an active compilation backend. If `mode=\"NONE\"`, this wrapper fails during EngineCore initialization, resulting in a cryptic error disconnected from the user's explicit configuration choices.\n\n**Fix:** Added a direct compatibility check in `vllm/engine/arg_utils.py:create_engine_config()` immediately after `speculative_config` and `compilation_config` are instantiated. This cleanly rejects the combination before the engine attempts to initialize devices.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>",
